The legal texts come from ZambiaLII (Southern African Institute for Policy and Research, on the Laws.Africa Peachjam platform):

  ZambiaLII, https://zambialii.org, point-in-time versions of each act, read from archived copies of its
  pages on the Internet Archive (https://web.archive.org), retrieved 2026-10-28.

ZambiaLII licenses its primary and secondary law content under the Creative Commons
Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International licence (CC BY-NC 4.0),
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/legalcode, and asks to be credited as the source
(https://zambialii.org/terms-of-use/, s. 9). Attribution:

  Source: ZambiaLII (https://zambialii.org), licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International licence (CC BY-NC 4.0).

The texts may be used only for non-commercial purposes.

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per
line; spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; editorial notes, Part and Chapter headings were left out;
and the versions were arranged as git commits credited to the laws ZambiaLII names for each change.
The wording of the law was not changed. Neither ZambiaLII nor Laws.Africa endorses this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the
tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
